Q: Java, How to add values to Array List used as value in HashMap (a multimap) A: <h2><code>computeIfAbsent</code></h2>
<p>Many of the other examples would fail with a NullPointerError if scores have not been initialized yet.</p>
<p>You can use <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/util/HashMap.html#computeIfAbsent(K,java.util.function.Function)" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>HashMap.computeIfAbsent</code></a>. See <a href="https://www.w3schools.com/java/ref_hashmap_computeifabsent.asp" rel="nofollow noreferrer">tutorial</a>.</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>Map&lt;String, ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;&gt; examList = new HashMap&lt;String, ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;&gt;();

ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; scores = examList.computeIfAbsent(&quot;A&quot;, course -&gt; new ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;());
scores.add(1);
scores.add(2);
scores.add(3);

scores = examList.computeIfAbsent(&quot;B&quot;, course -&gt; new ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;());
scores.add(11);
scores.add(12);
scores.add(13);

scores = examList.computeIfAbsent(&quot;A&quot;, course -&gt; new ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;());
scores.add(4);
scores.add(5);

System.out.println(examList);

</code></pre>
<p>It outputs:</p>
<pre><code>{A=[1, 2, 3, 4, 5], B=[11, 12, 13]}
</code></pre>
